<title>ARGENTINA: Perez authorized to expand bond program.</title>
<headline>Perez authorized to expand bond program.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine conglomerate Perez Companc was authorized to expand a medium-term global program to issue negotiable bonds to $1.2 billion from $800 million, the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange said Friday.</p>
<p>The program had initially been set at $500 million. ((-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
